@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy & Zero-Tracker Transparency";
}

<section class="legal-page">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
        <div class="legal-header">
            <div class="hero-tag">
                <span class="badge-tag badge-green">🛡️ Privacy &amp; Data Transparency</span>
            </div>
            <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
            <div class="legal-meta">
                <span>Effective Date: January 1, 2026</span>
                <span>Last Updated: September 1, 2026</span>
                <span>Compliance: GDPR • CCPA • Chrome Web Store Developer Agreement</span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-content">
            <div class="highlight-box">
                <strong>Executive Summary:</strong> Stream Helper operates on a privacy-respecting model. We do not sell your personal data, we do not employ third-party advertising tracking networks, and we never perform device fingerprinting or harvest browser history. Download history is stored exclusively for authenticated users to manage their personal downloads, and can be cleared at any time.
            </div>

            <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
            <p>We collect only the minimum information necessary to provide account services and download tracking:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Account Details:</strong> When you register an account or sign in with Google OAuth, we store your name, email address, password hash (salted via ASP.NET Core Identity PBKDF2), and creation date. We never ask for or store your Google password.</li>
                <li><strong>Download History:</strong> When signed in, your download history records the video title, source webpage URL (with temporary authorization tokens stripped), quality, format, file size, and download performance metrics so you can view and manage your downloads.</li>
                <li><strong>Session Cookies:</strong> We use secure, encrypted HTTP cookies strictly for authentication and security token validation (CSRF protection).</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>2. Information We Do NOT Collect</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>No Device Fingerprinting:</strong> We do NOT collect MAC addresses, hardware IDs, Canvas/WebGL fingerprints, or advertising identifiers.</li>
                <li><strong>No General Browsing History:</strong> The application and browser extension only process video stream manifests on pages where you explicitly trigger analysis.</li>
                <li><strong>No Third-Party Ad Trackers:</strong> Zero Google Analytics, Meta Pixels, or telemetry SDKs are embedded.</li>
                <li><strong>No Transmission of Account Data to Media Hosts:</strong> Third-party CDNs only receive standard stream requests; your account credentials are never shared.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>3. User Data Rights &amp; Deletion</h2>
            <p>You have full ownership of your data under GDPR and CCPA:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Purge Download History:</strong> You can delete any or all download records instantly from your <a asp-controller="Account" asp-action="Downloads" class="auth-link">Downloads Dashboard</a>.</li>
                <li><strong>Account Deletion:</strong> You can request full account erasure at any time by contacting our Grievance Officer.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>4. Security Architecture</h2>
            <p>All authentication communications utilize HTTPS with TLS 1.3 encryption. Passwords are never logged or stored in plaintext.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
